  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 28e85389ca13cb34c9d7a32ffdf6c81e, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::dialogueInfo
  herSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: cbd30b8a029bb484db2ccf39249c62a0, type: 3}
  youngHerSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d37118f979532b34ebf9111c40798c2d, type: 3}
  himSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 4cca0f018c3646245b697d0dcdd9617c, type: 3}
  teacherSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 9ae587bedf9ea1641a7f76b5f7d85a22, type: 3}
  npcSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 47d3254be5bf5e04e9cf8d5ae57941dc, type: 3}
  voidSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 9d31e64feccd9974d9a3ce2300ef31f1, type: 3}
  HerOpening1:
  - Owwww...My head....
  - "Huh? Where am I\u2026 what happened?"
  - "This place is dark\u2026 I can\u2019t see anything."
  - Hello???
  - ...
  - HELLO??!!!?!!!
  - ................................
  - Am I all alone here?
  VoidOpening1:
  - "Wow\u2026 you really came\u2026"
  - "I never thought I\u2019d see the day you finally came back here."
  - "After all, it\u2019s been quite a while since you\u2019ve given this place any
    thought\u2026"
  HerOpening2:
  - Huh? What is that supposed to mean? Where am I? And who are you?
  VoidOpening2:
  - "\u2026If you\u2019ve forgotten who I am, then we really do have a problem.\r\n
    And I\u2019m surprised you don\u2019t even recognize your own mind."
  - "But then again\u2026 you haven\u2019t really been you for a long time, have
    you? So I guess I shouldn\u2019t expect you to remember me either\u2026"
  - "Still\u2026 welcome back. I wish it looked nicer for you."
  - "I tried, you know. But\u2026 It\u2019s kind of up to you now."
  HerOpening3:
  - "Wait\u2014what? This is my mind?"
  - "But now that I think about it\u2026 I can\u2019t remember past that. Why was
    I getting married? And to whom? How did I even get here?! I feel like I don\u2019t
    even know myself anymore\u2026"
  - "And if this is my mind\u2026 why is it so dark\u2026 so broken?\r\nI need to
    get back\u2026"
  - How do I fix it? How do I go back?
  VoidOpening3:
  - "\u2026Wow. It\u2019s really worse than I thought, huh\u2026 You can\u2019t remember
    ANYTHING."
  - "And\u2026yeah\u2026This place has been falling apart for a long time, but recently,
    it\u2019s been disappearing faster and faster."
  - "Like it\u2019s finally\u2026 giving up."
  - "You\u2019ve lost sight of who you are, Her. And whatever choice you\u2019re
    about to make\u2026 It\u2019s pulling everything down with it."
  - "But\u2014hey, it\u2019s not over yet. There is a way out of this."
  - You just have to remember. Who you are.
  HerOpening4:
  - "Wait\u2014what? This is all happening so fast\u2026How do I even start?"
  VoidOpening4:
  - "Hehe\u2026 yeah, you always did hate not having a plan."
  - "Don\u2019t worry\u2014I\u2019m here with you! This can be fun!"
  - There are some doors that contain your memories somewhere around here. We will
    regain your memories one by one. We just have to go backwards.
  - "Let\u2019s start from where you are now\u2026 your adulthood.\r\nPiece by piece,
    we\u2019ll find what you lost."
  - "C\u2019mon now\u2014Go find that open door!"
  HerMazeIntro1:
  - What the? What is this place? This doesn't look like my memories...
  VoidMazeIntro1:
  - Hmm...It seems like you've been gone so long, your own mind doesn't recognize
    you anymore and has set up all these walls, like a protection system!
  - You probably have to FIND your memories before you can remember them again.
  - Ha! How clever! It may be inconvenient for us but I have to give good credit
    where it's due, this is a well built security system! Hahahaha!
  HerMazeIntro2:
  - Hey! I thought you were supposed to be on my side! This situation is by NO MEANS
    funny.
  VoidMazeIntro2:
  - Lighten up a little! I can be on your side while acknowledging good level design.
  HerMazeIntro3:
  - JUST GET TO THE POINT ALREADY. I'VE GOT A WEDDING TO GET BACK TO!
  VoidMazeIntro3:
  - Ughhhh... You're no funnnnn!
  - Fine fine, I guess we will RUSH this very rare out of body experience since you're
    so IMPATIENT! Tsk..Tsk.....
  - Well I mentioned that the place was falling apart right?
  - Well, all the places in your mind have become total total nonsense! Everything
    has gotten scrambled up and things faze in and out of existence within seconds!
  HerMazeIntro4:
  - HUH? What do you mean by that??? Scrambled...dissapearing...what?
  VoidMazeIntro4:
  - 'Well I guess you''ll have to see for yourself....... '
  - .....
  - What! You can't expect me to reveal EVERYTHING!
  - 'UGHHHHH FINE! All I''ll say is that you can use the fading parts of your mind
    to phase through obstructions and get places you couldn''t before. '
  - BUT THAT'S IT. You're getting NOTHING ELSE OUT OF ME!!!
  - ....for now.
  HerAdulthood1:
  - What.....What am I looking at?
  - Why is everything...scrambled...
  - Where even am I?
  VoidAdulthood1:
  - 'Well...remember when I said that all the places looked kinda...messed up? '
  - Well.....this is just the surface of it. There's places that look wayyyyy more
    confusing than this!
  - But this is a memory of you in your office. Your bigggg, corner office on the
    28th floor, everyone's dream...right?
  - 'Don''t you remember? Isn''t this the nice, stable life you always hoped for? '
  HerAdulthood2:
  - "Yes.........No??? \nI don't know...It's kind of hazy."
  - But, I mean, I just figured I would look more...
  - ....
  VoidAdulthood2:
  - more.....?
  HerAdulthood3:
  - I don't know. Happy? Bright? Satisfied and stable?
  - It just seems like I'm going in circles. Doing paperwork, staring, longing, and
    starting over.
  - And what even is that gigantic painting on the wall I keep looking at?
  - It looks like me and...is that...is that Him? The guy I'm marrying?
  VoidAdulthood3:
  - Yep...that's Him alright...looking...bright as ever. That's for sure.
  - I must say. You really do have...interesting taste in men. Not quite who I would
    have envisioned you settling for.
  HerAdulthood4:
  - Hey! What's that supposed to mean? I may not remember him but that's my husband-to-be!
  - Maybe he's not as bad as you think. I must have loved Him for a reason.
  VoidAdulthood4:
  - You don't even REMEMBER Him and you're on his side already?
  - I guess you're more entranced by Him than I remember. This is going to be harder
    than I thought...
  - But, anyway! Nevermind that comment. You'll come to learn about Him soon enough.
  - But yeah, this biggggg corner office in this big fancy building is his building.
    You work for him.
  HerAdulthood5:
  - I work FOR him? My husband-to-be? Are you sure?
  - That's not what I'd pictured for myself...there's no way.
  VoidAdulthood5:
  - I'm no mastermind but I'm pretty sure I'M the one giving the out-of-body experience
    tour of your memories here. I've got my facts straight.
  - And yes, you're his secretary.
  - You see, he's a very popular artist now. All thanks to you.
  - You helped him build his fame from the ground up and, now, he's got notoriety
    and multiple companies under his name.
  - He gets to make all the art and manage the creative projects and you...
  - 'YOU get to manage his checkbook! How EXCITING! '
  HerAdulthood6:
  - I'm sensing some sarcasm in there...but whatever.
  - I mean...that doesn't sound like the worst thing. I mean we manage a successful
    company together!
  - We must have made a good name for ourselves, Him and I.
  VoidAdulthood6:
  - Ooooh...except that it's all under HIS name. Not yours.
  - There's a reason he's out there in the limelight calling all the shots while
    you're crammed up in this dark, messy office organizing and filing everything
    that makes his world go 'round, paper after paper after paper.
  - 'But who am I to say that that''s not what you want, right. I mean just look
    at you! All busy and at work! '
  - Don't you just look so happy and content over there?
  HerAdulthood7:
  - Does it...get better?
  - Did I become happier?
  - Where is the next memory? Show me. Take me there now.
  VoidAdulthood7:
  - Woahhhh there, calm down. Your short term memories didn't last long before your
    mind started to give, they're as good as gone now.
  - 'I''m no fortune teller...but from what I remember you guys decided to tie the
    knot not long after this specific moment. '
  - You're parents were super happy and on board, going on and on about how it was
    about time you settle down anyway. Start focusing on the home life, your future
    family, and supporting Him more as a wife.
  - And based on what you're dressed in right now...I'm guessing you took engagement
    pictures soon after that and...
  - Well, here you are on your wedding day, probably unconcious in the back of the
    church or something.
  - Ha, that must be a fun sight to see. The bride passed out in the back of the
    church before her supposed best day of her life! I'd love to see THAT! HAHAHA!
  VoidAdulthood7Pt2:
  - ...
  - Hey, you gotta admit that one was a little funny. No laughs at all?
  - ...
  - Alright, what's going on. Out with it.
  HerAdulthood8:
  - I just....
  - I just can't believe I could ever do this to myself.
  - Put myself in this situation.
  - I'm not that weak.
  - ...
  - Am I?
  - What...What do you want me to take from this?
  - That my life is all wrong? That I'm making a mistake? What is the point of this
    experiment? Are you trying to mess with me?
  VoidAdulthood8:
  - Hey hey don't shoot the messenger. I'm just a figure of your consciousness here
    to guide you.
  - There's no right or wrong answer to this. This is your journey.
  - All I'm asking is that you have the strength to see, to understand, and to realize.
  - Are you starting to see?
  HerAdulthood9:
  - I...
  - I'm starting to...
  - But everything is so hazy, it's just hard to take it all in at once.
  VoidAdulthood9:
  - That's alright, this is progress!
  - We've got allllll the time in the world. After all, this is your own consciousness.
    Time gets all loopy in here! Tehehehe.
  HimAdulthood1:
  - HER! HURRY UP. I've been waiting for 20 minutes it can't take that long.
  - I've been working all day, a man needs his rest and a good homemade dinner from
    his woman.
  - Come down to the car already!
  VoidAdulthood10:
  - Oops! Looks like she dropped something. Go check what it is. I'm nosy I wanna
    see.
  VoidEndAdulthood1:
  - 'Ooooooooh it''s a pair of scissors! '
  - And would you look at that, it seems you've gained your insight back!
  HerEndAdulthood1:
  - Gained my insight back? What does that mean? How do you know for sure?
  - And what am I even supposed to do with these scissors?
  VoidEndAdulthood2:
  - Well, you see that nifty, difty monitor up there in the top left? You've got
    your scissors and a light bulb there now, which symbolize your possessions and
    traits!
  - And gaining your insight back means you will be able to think faster and move
    quicker!
  - It's a sign that you are beginning to see more clearly. But this is just the
    start, we still have a while to go to save this place from destruction.
  - And, I'm no genius, but I imagine scissors can cut through ropes...
  - Maybe you could, and I'm just spit balling here, use it to cut some rope barriers
    and get to places you couldn't before...
  HerEndAdulthood2:
  - Ha. Ha. Ha. Touche. I'll keep it in mind.
  - Where to now?
  VoidEndAdulthood3:
  - Haha! There's that sense of humor starting to come back!
  - Well, your past self so kindly left us an exit back to your main mindscape, so
    let's follow it out and go backwards in your memories some more...
  - The next stage is your DREADED TEENS. DUN. DUN. DUNNNNNN.
  - ....
  - What. Was that one not to your tastes?
  VoidDemoLines:
  - Hello there, kind player! I am The Void (but who am I truly? We don't quite know
    yet...)
  - I just wanted to make the disclaimer that this is where the in-depth cutscenes
    end, as the developers of "Hitched" are still working on the next ones!
  - Otherwise, please press Shift + R to go back to the menu scene and restart the
    experience for the next player!
  - This is just the start of mine and Her's journey through her memories, so make
    sure to aniticpate our final release! There is so much more story to tell.
  - Until next time!
